Crops, South China Agricultural University, Guangzhou, China."}]}},{"fullName":"Hou Z","lastName":"Hou","firstName":"Zhuangwei","initials":"Z","authorAffiliationDetailsList":{"authorAffiliation":[{"affiliation":"Shenzhen Branch, Guangdong Laboratory for Lingnan Modern Agriculture, Genome Analysis Laboratory of the Ministry of Agriculture, Agricultural Genomics Institute at Shenzhen, Chinese Academy of Agricultural Sciences, Shenzhen, China."}]}},{"fullName":"Shi F","lastName":"Shi","firstName":"Fenghou","initials":"F","authorAffiliationDetailsList":{"authorAffiliation":[{"affiliation":"State Key Laboratory of Tree Genetics and Breeding, Co-Innovation Center for Sustainable Forestry in Southern China, College of Forestry and Grassland, Nanjing Forestry University, Nanjing, China."}]}},{"fullName":"Wang Z","lastName":"Wang","firstName":"Zefu","initials":"Z","authorAffiliationDetailsList":{"authorAffiliation":[{"affiliation":"College of Ecology and Environment, Nanjing Forestry University, Nanjing, China."}]}},{"fullName":"Yang W","lastName":"Yang","firstName":"Wenjie","initials":"W","authorAffiliationDetailsList":{"authorAffiliation":[{"affiliation":"College of Ecology and Environment, Nanjing Forestry University, Nanjing, China."}]}},{"fullName":"Shen Y","lastName":"Shen","firstName":"Yongbao","initials":"Y","authorAffiliationDetailsList":{"authorAffiliation":[{"affiliation":"State Key Laboratory of Tree Genetics and Breeding, Co-Innovation Center for Sustainable Forestry in Southern China, College of Forestry and Grassland, Nanjing Forestry University, Nanjing, China."}]}}]},"authorIdList":{"authorId":[{"type":"ORCID","value":"0000-0002-6446-8812"}]},"journalInfo":{"issue":"3","volume":"19","journalIssueId":4222847,"dateOfPublication":"2026 Sep","monthOfPublication":9,"yearOfPublication":2026,"journal":{"medlineAbbreviation":"Plant Genome","title":"The plant genome","essn":"1940-3372","issn":"1940-3372","nlmid":"101273919","isoabbreviation":"Plant Genome"},"printPublicationDate":"2026-09-01"},"pubYear":"2026","pageInfo":"e70286","abstractText":"Callery pear (Pyrus calleryana) is a deciduous species native to East Asia with notable ornamental and ecological value, but the genomic resources for this species remain limited. Here, we report the first haplotype-resolved, chromosome-scale genome of P. calleryana. The final genome assembly comprises two phased haplotypes measuring 506.97 and 504.62 Mb. These haplotypes contain 41,234 and 41,329 predicted protein-coding genes, respectively, with more than 97% of the genes receiving functional annotations. Comparative genomic analyses further identified 680 species-specific orthogroups enriched in hormone signaling, metabolic processes, and stress-responsive pathways, among which several LIK1-like genes may contribute to environmental adaptation. This high-quality genome assembly offers an essential foundation for subsequent studies on the ecological adaptability, invasiveness, and functional genomics of P. calleryana.","affiliation":"State Key Laboratory of Tree Genetics and Breeding, Co-Innovation Center for Sustainable Forestry in Southern China, College of Forestry and Grassland, Nanjing Forestry University, Nanjing, China.","publicationStatus":"ppublish","language":"eng","pubModel":"Print","pubTypeList":{"pubType":["other","Journal Article"]},"grantsList":{"grant":[{"agency":"National Natural Science Foundation of China","grantId":"32422053","orderIn":0},{"agency":"Central Finance Forestry Science and Technology Extension and Demonstration Fund","grantId":"Su[2024]TG07","orderIn":0},{"agency":"Natural Science Foundation of Jiangsu Province","grantId":"BK20230394","orderIn":0}]},"meshHeadingList":{"meshHeading":[{"majorTopic_YN":"Y","descriptorName":"Pyrus","meshQualifierList":{"meshQualifier":[{"majorTopic_YN":"N","abbreviation":"GE","qualifierName":"genetics"}]}},{"majorTopic_YN":"Y","descriptorName":"Adaptation, Physiological","meshQualifierList":{"meshQualifier":[{"majorTopic_Y